# baseline-access — committed key list (values live in your shell, NOT in git).
#
# Bitwarden auth on first boot is interactive (email + master password + 2FA);
# no Bitwarden env vars are needed or supported in this cut.
#
# Optional: pre-set your git identity to skip the interactive prompt.
#
# Recommended convention:
#   GIT_IDENTITY_NAME   your GitHub username            e.g. octocat
#   GIT_IDENTITY_EMAIL  your GitHub noreply address     e.g. octocat@users.noreply.github.com
#
# The noreply address keeps your real email out of public commit history while
# GitHub still attributes the commits to your account. Find yours under
# GitHub -> Settings -> Emails (newer accounts use <ID>+<username>@users.noreply.github.com).
GIT_IDENTITY_NAME=
GIT_IDENTITY_EMAIL=

# Future extension (NOT implemented yet): unattended Bitwarden auth via API key.
#   BW_CLIENTID=
#   BW_CLIENTSECRET=
